  overview: [
    "On light glass, the description and currency prefix use the stronger foreground color. For custom body content, use the default `Typography` foreground for message copy over the dimmed background.",
    "Browser Escape and the system back cancel the foremost open child overlay before the dialog. Cancelling the dialog calls `onCancel` and requests `open=false`, including destructive dialogs and dialogs with custom children. A controlled owner may keep it open; that request never confirms an action.",
    "Pass `dismissible` to let a backdrop press follow the same cancel policy. It is off by default, so existing dialogs and destructive confirmations keep their current outside-press behavior. The scrim is excluded from keyboard navigation.",
    "Use `form overlay dismissible` for the original Argus application dialog: a persistent title and optional `description`, a close action, and scrolling body and `footer` content. `panelWidth` bounds the form (560 pixels by default), and the viewport keeps a twenty-pixel safe-area inset. The web treatment preserves Argus’s 28-pixel content inset, 17-pixel title, rounded card, shadow, and lightly frosted dim. A form with no trigger contributes no layout wrapper to its caller. Nested menus receive Escape before the dialog; focus stays in the open modal.",
    "For a conversation or other workspace with its own scroll region, use `form workspace overlay`. The dialog measures a safe-area-bounded viewport height; its header and optional `footer` stay fixed while `children` fill the remaining space. Put the workspace's scrollable content inside `children` and keep its composer or other controls as siblings of that scroll region. The workspace body does not add an outer scrollport. `workspaceHeader` adds content below the title and description in the fixed header, such as a step indicator. This mode is intended for an overlay form; ordinary forms keep their existing scrolling body.",
    "Add `compact` to a workspace when short content should determine the panel's height: `form workspace compact overlay`. The panel hugs the conversation and composer, then grows up to the same safe-area-bounded viewport maximum. A long conversation scrolls inside its own thread while the header, composer, and dialog footer remain visible. The default workspace still fills its available height; `compact` has no effect without `form workspace`.",
    "Add `embedded` to show an open dialog in a page as a specimen, the way a catalogue or a showcase does: it keeps its look, its dialog role and its labelling, but it is not modal. It does not take focus when it opens, trap Tab, return focus, set `aria-modal`, or cancel on Escape, native back or a backdrop press, so the page around it keeps its scroll position and its keyboard order. `embedded` is ignored with `trigger`, which always opens a live modal.",
  ],
